.TH DN 1 "" "Directory Navigator" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dn \- terminal file manager inspired by DOS Navigator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dn
.RB [ \-\-no-session ]
.br
.B dn
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Directory Navigator provides two file panes, movable windows, text viewers and
editors, archive browsing, remote connections, and music playback.
Run it from the directory you want to browse in a terminal of at least 80 columns
and 25 rows. Press F1 for the built-in help.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no-session
Start in the launch directory without restoring the previous session.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dn
Configuration and persistent application data. Defaults to
.I ~/.config/dn
when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset.
.SH DOCUMENTATION
The user guide and third-party notices are installed in
.IR /usr/share/doc/directory-navigator/ .
.SH AUTHORS
Dmitry Yarygin and contributors.
